  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 358 AM MDT THU AUG 20 2026\nDry air behind the front will limit shower and thunderstorm \ndevelopment to the ID/NV border area and eastern Boise Mtns on \nSunday. Temperatures will run 4-8 degrees cooler than Saturday,\nplacing lower elevations around 90 degrees, which is near normal\nheading into late August. For next week, we'll remain on the\nnorthwest fringe of a broad ridge centered over NM. Early in the\nweek flow around the ridge will keep moisture over southern and \neastern areas, supporting a 20-40% chance of showers and \nthunderstorms over higher terrain of southwest Idaho. By \nWednesday drier air will cut off precipitation chances for most\nareas. Temperatures are back above normal next week.",
